

-> @RequestBody & JSON → Java

    @PostMapping("/users")
    public User create(@RequestBody UserDTO dto)

    Reads JSON request body
    Converts to Java object
    Uses Jackson

-> Role of Jackson
    Jackson:
    Converts JSON → Java (Deserialization)
    Converts Java → JSON (Serialization)
    📌 Automatic in Spring Boot


-> @ResponseBody

    @ResponseBody
    public User getUser() {}

    Converts return value to JSON
    Included automatically in @RestController

-> Handling invalid JSON

    If JSON is invalid:
    Spring throws HttpMessageNotReadableException
    Returns 400 Bad Request
    📌 Can be handled using @ExceptionHandler


